<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Sample SpiceGrinder model: credit card number via the CreditCard generator (default mode).

  Network is a plain composed Input drawn from creditcard_networks_weighted.csv — real US
  credit-card network market share (Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Discover), weighted
  by real purchase-volume percentages. Remaining digits between each network's real BIN
  prefix and the check digit are filled in at random and a valid Luhn check digit is
  computed, so the result is format- and checksum-valid but not derived from any real
  cardholder's actual account.

  Fully random by default, not restricted to the guaranteed-safe published test numbers —
  confirmed directly with the user rather than assumed ("Credit card. Same design ethic:
  truly random with an approved fake option."). This means a generated number can, in
  principle, coincide with a real, currently-issued card — but it carries zero connection to
  any real person or PII. If a guaranteed-non-colliding number is needed instead, set
  fictionalOnly="true" on the CreditCard node below to substitute each network's real,
  published test number (the exact same numbers Stripe, and every other major payment
  processor, documents for sandbox testing) — at the cost of zero variety, since every draw
  for a given network is then identical.

  Output: one Observation of [card] per pull, rendered as "4242 4242 4242 4242"
  (CreditCardDataPoint's default grouped format).
-->
<dataset>
	<root node="PaymentCard"/>
	<nodes>
		<CreditCard name="PaymentCard">
			<input name="Network"/>
		</CreditCard>

		<FlatFile name="Network"
			file="samples/pro/creditcard_networks_weighted.csv"
			mode="weighted"/>
	</nodes>
</dataset>
